INGESTION TERMS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Term: ActivityMinute
Definition: "Timestamp representing
exact minute when Fitbit device
recorded biometric measurement
Format: MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM:SS AM/PM"
Owner: Data Engineering Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Steps
Definition: "Number of steps taken
by user in one minute period
Valid range: 0-200 steps/minute
Source: Fitbit accelerometer"
Owner: Data Engineering Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Calories
Definition: "Calories burned by user
in one minute period
Valid range: 0-20 calories/minute
Unit: kilocalories (kcal)"
Owner: Data Engineering Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Intensity
Definition: "Physical activity intensity
level recorded per minute
Valid values: 0,1,2,3
0=Sedentary, 1=Light
2=Moderate, 3=Very Active"
Owner: Data Engineering Team
Status: Approved 

Term: MET
Definition: "Metabolic Equivalent of Task
Measure of exercise intensity
1 MET = energy at rest
Values above 3 = moderate activity"
Owner: Data Science Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Sleep Value
Definition: "Sleep stage recorded
per minute by Fitbit device
1=Asleep, 2=Restless, 3=Awake"
Owner: Data Engineering Team
Status: Approved 

DERIVED TERMS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Term: Anomaly Score
Definition: "ML-generated probability
score indicating likelihood of
fraudulent step-count activity
Range: 0.0 to 1.0
Threshold: >0.8 = fraud suspected"
Owner: Data Science Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Health Risk Level
Definition: "User health risk category
derived from WHO physical activity
guidelines
Values: LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH"
Owner: Analytics Team
Status: Approved 

Term: Active Minutes
Definition: "Total minutes per day
where steps > 10
WHO target: 30+ active minutes/day"
Owner: Analytics Team
Status: Approved 

Term: User ID (Masked)
Definition: "SHA-256 hashed user
identifier replacing original
Fitbit device ID for HIPAA-adjacent
PII compliance
Format: USR_XXXXXXXX"
Owner: Data Governance Team
Status: Approved 

POLICY TERMS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━
Term: PHI (Protected Health Information)
Definition: "Any health data that
can identify an individual user
Includes: user_id, device_id
Must be masked before Silver layer"
Owner: Compliance Team
Status: Approved 

Term: PII (Personally Identifiable Information)
Definition: "Data that can identify
specific individual
In this project: original user_id
Must be SHA-256 hashed at ingestion"
Owner: Compliance Team
Status: Approved 
